WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.356
Cheap grain through ration shops

2
00:00:02.356 --> 00:00:03.171
is old.

3
00:00:03.171 --> 00:00:05.821
Making it a legal entitlement

4
00:00:05.821 --> 00:00:07.567
came in 2013.

5
00:00:07.903 --> 00:00:09.569
The Act covers up to

6
00:00:09.569 --> 00:00:11.447
75 percent of the rural

7
00:00:11.447 --> 00:00:13.534
population and up to 50

8
00:00:13.534 --> 00:00:16.219
percent of the urban population.

9
00:00:16.577 --> 00:00:18.932
Priority households get 5 kilograms

10
00:00:18.932 --> 00:00:20.430
of grain per person,

11
00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:21.566
every month.

12
00:00:21.566 --> 00:00:22.579
The poorest,

13
00:00:22.579 --> 00:00:24.180
Antyodaya households,

14
00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:26.914
get 35 kilograms per household.

15
00:00:27.269 --> 00:00:29.160
Pregnant women and mothers get

16
00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:30.770
a maternity benefit of at

17
00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:32.691
least six thousand rupees.

18
00:00:32.691 --> 00:00:34.589
And children get meals through

19
00:00:34.589 --> 00:00:36.538
anganwadis and schools.

20
00:00:36.877 --> 00:00:38.148
Your turn.

21
00:00:38.148 --> 00:00:39.972
How much for an Antyodaya

22
00:00:39.972 --> 00:00:41.191
household?
